## Make this your own!

The most sensitive controls are $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$, so small parameter sweeps around the creature are a good next experiment. One can also replace the initial field, change the ring amplitudes $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$, or track the mass and centroid over time.

See you next time!

## References

- B. W.-C. Chan, [*Lenia—Biology of Artificial Life*](https://doi.org/10.25088/ComplexSystems.28.3.251), *Complex Systems* **28**(3), 251–286 (2019). [Open-access preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.05433).
- B. W.-C. Chan, [*Lenia and Expanded Universe*](https://doi.org/10.1162/isal_a_00297), *Artificial Life Conference Proceedings* **32**, 221–229 (2020). [Open-access preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.03742).
- S. Rafler, [*Generalization of Conway's Game of Life to a Continuous Domain—SmoothLife*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.1567) (2011).
- [Lenia project page](https://chakazul.github.io/lenia.html) and [reference implementations](https://github.com/Chakazul/Lenia).

